          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "સોજો — sojo — \"swelling\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "શું તમારા પગમાં સોજો છે? — śũ tamārā pagmā̃ sojo che? — \"Is there swelling in your foot?\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "સોજો (sojo) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. CDIAL lists it, glossed \"a swelling\", under śūyate, \"is swollen\" (CDIAL 12568)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
